{
  "finalText": "Fixed. The bug was on line 19 of `utils/pages.py`:\n\n```python\nreturn [items[i] for i in range(start, end - 1) if 0 <= i < len(items)]\n```\n\nThe `end - 1` cut the range one short. With `PAGE_SIZE = 10`, page 0 spans `range(0, 9)` → 9 items instead of 10. Changed it to `range(start, end)`, which yields exactly `PAGE_SIZE` indices per page.\n\nI couldn't run the Python verification — the interpreter call needs approval in this session, so I didn't execute it. The fix is correct by inspection: `range(start, start + PAGE_SIZE)` yields exactly 10 indices, and the `0 <= i < len(items)` guard still trims the final partial page correctly. If you want, approve the command and I'll confirm end-to-end.\n\nOne unrelated thing I noticed while in the file: the module docstring (line 4) says pages are \"20 items each,\" but `PAGE_SIZE = 10`. That's a stale comment, not a behavior bug — want me to correct it too?",
